  "sweep_label": "A100, GPU energy only",
  "sweep_provenance": "Grace job 20190061, Oct 18 2026; NVIDIA A100 PCIe 40 GB, 250 W, driver 580.126.20; vLLM 0.21.0 (GN100 runs 0.23), torch 2.11.0+cu130; Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-FP8 (config.json sha256 002ebe91531ec67011b3d0c923234ef708c7da7d3b246045c4475d90b3d94628), FP8 weights with 16 bit compute (Marlin kernel); prefix caching on; contexts of random vocabulary tokens, not real prompts; 64 output tokens, greedy, ignore_eos; FlashInfer sampler off (VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0, PyTorch native sampler); energy from NVML nvmlDeviceGetTotalEnergyConsumption, GPU board only, idle power subtracted (32.6 W start, 36.1 W end); 6 contexts x cached and uncached x 10 repeats = 120 calls, shuffled; no A-LEMS, no store.",
  "sweep_fit_method": "e(c) = a + b c + d c^2 on net joules per call, c = prompt tokens / 1000, least squares on all repeats; 95 percent percentile intervals from 2000 bootstrap draws resampling repeats within each context, seed 0. Per 1k slopes: straight line on contexts 2k to 16k and on 16k to 32k. Preregistered rule: 'faster than linear' only if the d interval excludes 0 (uncached: excludes 0; cached: includes 0).",
  "units": "Laya values are fractions (Brier scores, Brier differences, probabilities, p values); counts are integers; no percents. Sweep values carry their unit in kind (joules, joules per 1k tokens, ratio, fraction).",
  "sign_convention": "Differences are learned minus Beta; negative favours the learned model. display carries an explicit + for positive differences.",
  "ci_method": "Paired bootstrap over tasks: 1000 draws (BOOT = 1000), each draw resamples whole tasks with replacement and scores both methods on the same rows; 95 percent interval from the 2.5 and 97.5 percentiles; seed 7 (eval seed); laya_eval.brier_diff_ci. Out of fold predictions, 5 folds grouped by task, seed 0. Pool intervals are not corrected for multiple comparisons.",
